a kept-alive connection: answered #t, then closed when idle
a body too slow: cut off, answered #f
a body given longer by its handler: got 100
a client reading none of 32 MB: dropped before the end #t
a small body left unread: read past, and the connection answers again
a large body left unread: answered #t, then closed
a client still sending after a 413: read it #t, then closed
a body to come once told to continue: answered #t, closed before the request's timeout #t
